export default {"T000184":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"implies\" data-relation-style=\"implication\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Implication</span><h3>Finitely presented module ⇒ Finite module</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All premises</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000143\"><span>Finitely presented module</span><code>P000143</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../topologies/database/#T000184\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T000184</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇒</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All conclusions</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000142\"><span>Finite module</span><code>P000142</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Modules</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> The presentation includes a surjection from a finite free module.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0518\">Stacks 0518 · original statement</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/algebra/#tag-0518\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://www.jmilne.org/math/xnotes/CA.pdf#page=52\">J. S. Milne, A Primer of Commutative Algebra, v4.03, Definition 12.2 (the finite set of module generators in a presentation)</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T000184\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../topologies/database/#T000184\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","T000185":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"implies\" data-relation-style=\"implication\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Implication</span><h3>Free module ⇒ Projective module</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All premises</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000144\"><span>Free module</span><code>P000144</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../topologies/database/#T000185\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T000185</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇒</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All conclusions</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000149\"><span>Projective module</span><code>P000149</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Modules</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> A lift against a surjective map can be chosen on each basis vector.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05CE\">Stacks 05CE · original statement</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/algebra/#tag-05CE\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://www.jmilne.org/math/xnotes/CA.pdf#page=51\">J. S. Milne, A Primer of Commutative Algebra, v4.03, §12, following Definition 12.1 (arbitrary direct sums of copies of the ring)</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T000185\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../topologies/database/#T000185\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","T000186":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"implies\" data-relation-style=\"implication\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Implication</span><h3>Free module ⇒ Flat module</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All premises</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000144\"><span>Free module</span><code>P000144</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../topologies/database/#T000186\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T000186</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇒</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All conclusions</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000153\"><span>Flat module</span><code>P000153</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Modules</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> Tensoring with a free module gives a direct sum of copies of the input. Direct sums preserve exact sequences.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00HB\">Stacks 00HB · original statement</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/algebra/#tag-00HB\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://www.jmilne.org/math/xnotes/CA.pdf#page=45\">J. S. Milne, A Primer of Commutative Algebra, v4.03, Example 11.3 (arbitrary free modules)</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T000186\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../topologies/database/#T000186\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","T000187":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"equivalence\" data-relation-style=\"equivalence\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Equivalence</span><h3>Finite module ∧ Free module ⇔ Finite free module</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Left conditions (all)</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000142\"><span>Finite module</span><code>P000142</code></a><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000144\"><span>Free module</span><code>P000144</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../topologies/database/#T000187\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T000187</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇔</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Right conditions (all)</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000145\"><span>Finite free module</span><code>P000145</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Modules</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> If the base ring is nonzero, an infinite free basis cannot be generated by finitely many vectors with finite support. Over the zero ring the module is zero and admits the empty basis.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00C2\">Stacks 00C2 · original statement</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/algebra/#tag-00C2\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T000187\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../topologies/database/#T000187\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","T000188":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"equivalence\" data-relation-style=\"equivalence\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Equivalence</span><h3>Projective module ⇔ Direct summand of a free module</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Left conditions (all)</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000149\"><span>Projective module</span><code>P000149</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../topologies/database/#T000188\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T000188</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇔</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Right conditions (all)</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000151\"><span>Direct summand of a free module</span><code>P000151</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Modules</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> A surjection from a free module onto a projective module splits, and a summand of a projective module is projective.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05CF\">Stacks 05CF · original statement</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/algebra/#tag-05CF\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://www.jmilne.org/math/xnotes/CA.pdf#page=51\">J. S. Milne, A Primer of Commutative Algebra, v4.03, §12, following Definition 12.1 (free summands of arbitrary rank characterize projectives)</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T000188\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../topologies/database/#T000188\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","T000189":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"implies\" data-relation-style=\"implication\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Implication</span><h3>Projective module ⇒ Flat module</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All premises</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000149\"><span>Projective module</span><code>P000149</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../topologies/database/#T000189\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T000189</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇒</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All conclusions</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000153\"><span>Flat module</span><code>P000153</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Modules</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> Projectivity implies flatness by the characterization. Equivalently, a direct summand of a flat module is flat.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/059Z\">Stacks 059Z · original statement</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/algebra/#tag-059Z\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://www.jmilne.org/math/xnotes/CA.pdf#page=53\">J. S. Milne, A Primer of Commutative Algebra, v4.03, Theorem 12.6, proof of (a) ⇒ (d), using Example 11.3 for arbitrary direct summands</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T000189\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../topologies/database/#T000189\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","T000190":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"equivalence\" data-relation-style=\"equivalence\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Equivalence</span><h3>Finite module ∧ Projective module ⇔ Finite projective module</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Left conditions (all)</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000142\"><span>Finite module</span><code>P000142</code></a><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000149\"><span>Projective module</span><code>P000149</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../topologies/database/#T000190\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T000190</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇔</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Right conditions (all)</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000150\"><span>Finite projective module</span><code>P000150</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Modules</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> This is the finite-generation and projectivity condition together.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00NX\">Stacks 00NX · original statement</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/algebra/#tag-00NX\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T000190\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../topologies/database/#T000190\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","T000191":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"equivalence\" data-relation-style=\"equivalence\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Equivalence</span><h3>Finitely presented module ∧ Flat module ⇔ Finite projective module</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Left conditions (all)</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000143\"><span>Finitely presented module</span><code>P000143</code></a><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000153\"><span>Flat module</span><code>P000153</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../topologies/database/#T000191\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T000191</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇔</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Right conditions (all)</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000150\"><span>Finite projective module</span><code>P000150</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Modules</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> The finite-projective-module theorem identifies these two conditions.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00NX\">Stacks 00NX · original statement</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/algebra/#tag-00NX\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/058R\">Stacks 058R · original statement</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/algebra/#tag-058R\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://www.jmilne.org/math/xnotes/CA.pdf#page=53\">J. S. Milne, A Primer of Commutative Algebra, v4.03, Theorem 12.6(a),(d) (finite projectivity and flat finite presentation)</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T000191\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../topologies/database/#T000191\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","T000192":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"equivalence\" data-relation-style=\"equivalence\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Equivalence</span><h3>Finite projective module ⇔ Direct summand of a finite free module</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Left conditions (all)</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000150\"><span>Finite projective module</span><code>P000150</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../topologies/database/#T000192\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T000192</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇔</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Right conditions (all)</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000152\"><span>Direct summand of a finite free module</span><code>P000152</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Modules</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> Projectivity splits a finite free surjection, and a summand of a finite free module is finite projective.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00NX\">Stacks 00NX · original statement</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/algebra/#tag-00NX\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://www.jmilne.org/math/xnotes/CA.pdf#page=53\">J. S. Milne, A Primer of Commutative Algebra, v4.03, §12, immediately before Theorem 12.6 (summands of finite free modules)</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T000192\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../topologies/database/#T000192\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","T000193":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"equivalence\" data-relation-style=\"equivalence\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Equivalence</span><h3>Finite projective module ⇔ Finite locally free module</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Left conditions (all)</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000150\"><span>Finite projective module</span><code>P000150</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../topologies/database/#T000193\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T000193</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇔</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Right conditions (all)</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000147\"><span>Finite locally free module</span><code>P000147</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Modules</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> A finite projective module is finite locally free. Conversely, finite local freeness gives finite presentation and flatness.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00NX\">Stacks 00NX · original statement</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/algebra/#tag-00NX\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://www.jmilne.org/math/xnotes/CA.pdf#page=53\">J. S. Milne, A Primer of Commutative Algebra, v4.03, Theorem 12.6(a),(c) (finite free trivializations on a principal open cover)</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T000193\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../topologies/database/#T000193\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","T000194":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"implies\" data-relation-style=\"implication\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Implication</span><h3>Finite locally free module of a prescribed rank ⇒ Finite locally free module</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All premises</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000148\"><span>Finite locally free module of a prescribed rank</span><code>P000148</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../topologies/database/#T000194\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T000194</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇒</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All conclusions</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000147\"><span>Finite locally free module</span><code>P000147</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Modules</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> Use the same principal open covering and forget the fixed value of the rank.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00NW\">Stacks 00NW · original statement</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/algebra/#tag-00NW\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T000194\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../topologies/database/#T000194\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","T000195":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"implies\" data-relation-style=\"implication\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Implication</span><h3>Finite locally free module ⇒ Locally free module</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All premises</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000147\"><span>Finite locally free module</span><code>P000147</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../topologies/database/#T000195\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T000195</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇒</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All conclusions</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000146\"><span>Locally free module</span><code>P000146</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Modules</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> Use the same principal open covering and forget the finiteness of the rank.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00NW\">Stacks 00NW · original statement</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/algebra/#tag-00NW\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T000195\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../topologies/database/#T000195\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","T000196":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"implies\" data-relation-style=\"implication\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Implication</span><h3>Locally free module ⇒ Flat module</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All premises</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000146\"><span>Locally free module</span><code>P000146</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../topologies/database/#T000196\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T000196</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇒</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All conclusions</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000153\"><span>Flat module</span><code>P000153</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Modules</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> Each localization at a maximal ideal is free, hence flat.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00HT\">Stacks 00HT · original statement</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/algebra/#tag-00HT\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T000196\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../topologies/database/#T000196\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","T000197":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"implies\" data-relation-style=\"implication\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Implication</span><h3>Module over a local ring ∧ Finite module ∧ Flat module ⇒ Finite free module</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All premises</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000159\"><span>Module over a local ring</span><code>P000159</code></a><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000142\"><span>Finite module</span><code>P000142</code></a><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000153\"><span>Flat module</span><code>P000153</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../topologies/database/#T000197\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T000197</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇒</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All conclusions</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000145\"><span>Finite free module</span><code>P000145</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Modules</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> Lift a basis of the residue fibre. Nakayama gives a surjection, and flatness makes the lifted family a basis.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00NZ\">Stacks 00NZ · original statement</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/algebra/#tag-00NZ\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T000197\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../topologies/database/#T000197\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","T000198":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"implies\" data-relation-style=\"implication\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Implication</span><h3>Module over a local ring ∧ Projective module ⇒ Free module</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All premises</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000159\"><span>Module over a local ring</span><code>P000159</code></a><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000149\"><span>Projective module</span><code>P000149</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../topologies/database/#T000198\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T000198</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇒</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All conclusions</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000144\"><span>Free module</span><code>P000144</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Modules</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> Kaplansky’s theorem applies without finite-generation assumptions.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0593\">Stacks 0593 · original statement</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/algebra/#tag-0593\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T000198\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../topologies/database/#T000198\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","T000199":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"implies\" data-relation-style=\"implication\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Implication</span><h3>Module over a Noetherian ring ∧ Finite module ⇒ Finitely presented module</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All premises</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000160\"><span>Module over a Noetherian ring</span><code>P000160</code></a><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000142\"><span>Finite module</span><code>P000142</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../topologies/database/#T000199\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T000199</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇒</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All conclusions</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000143\"><span>Finitely presented module</span><code>P000143</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Modules</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> The kernel of a finite free presentation is a submodule of a finite module over a Noetherian ring, hence finite.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00FP\">Stacks 00FP · original statement</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/algebra/#tag-00FP\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T000199\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../topologies/database/#T000199\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>"};
